          "type": "text",
          "text": "## Sorting\n\nUse **sorted()** or *list.sort()*, with `key=` for custom order. See [the docs](https://docs.python.org/3/howto/sorting.html).\n\n- `sorted()` returns a new list\n  - works on any iterable\n- `list.sort()` sorts in place\n\n3. first step\n4. second step\n\n```python\nnums = [3, 1, 2]\nprint(sorted(nums))  # [1, 2, 3]\n```\n\n| Method | Returns |\n|---|---|\n| `sorted()` | new list |\n| `list.sort()` | None |\n\nEnergy: $E = mc^2$, and:\n\n$$\\sum_{i=1}^n i = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$$\n\n> Sorting is stable.\n\n---\n\nDone.",
